      "message": "test(machine): pin that a machine switch is judged again at the post\n\nTrace for #1241: an op generated on machine A, then remounted onto a\nmachine B whose limits it breaks - through the setup's own machine\n(SetSetupMachine) and, separately, the document's (LoadMachine). For\nthe stroke, the spindle top, a tilting rotary and the machine's kind,\nthe post re-judges the cached path against B and refuses by name,\nwriting nothing; undo puts A back and it posts, redo and save/reopen\nkeep B's refusal. The op stays Ok by the M2.3 roomy-one law (machine\nlimits are live gate inputs, never stamp inputs), recorded in\ndocs/decisions/1241-machine-switch-live-gate.md. No product change:\nno path cleared on A posts on B unjudged.\n\nFixes #1241\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
